<h2 class="section__title">What this site is</h2>
<p>CarSpecFix is a free reference that compiles U.S.-market vehicle specifications (engine oil, tire size and pressure, fuel economy, safety recalls) and plain-English explanations of common trouble codes and symptoms. Every figure is cited to an owner's manual, NHTSA or fueleconomy.gov. The site is supported by advertising.</p>
<p>You do not need an account, and there is nothing to buy. <strong>There is no download function and no software to install</strong> — everything is a web page you read in a browser.</p>

<h2 class="section__title">What it is not</h2>
<p>We are data compilers, not mechanics, dealers or lawyers. The site is not professional mechanical, safety or legal advice, and it is not a substitute for the owner's manual that came with your vehicle. Manufacturer procedures and specifications change by year, engine and market; always confirm a figure against your own manual before you act on it. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for detail.</p>

